# A copy of a Room is a Room whose doors are locked (CR 709.5d, 707.2): the existence of each half is part of the copiable
# values (CR 709.5b), but the unlocked designations are not, and a permanent that did not enter as a cast spell has neither.
# Faithless Looting discards Unholy Annex // Ritual Chamber and a Swamp, so the graveyard has four card types (delirium: an
# enchantment, a sorcery, an artifact from Black Lotus, a land), and Shifting Woodland becomes a copy of the Room card: an
# enchantment with no name, no mana cost, no abilities but the unlocks, and no door unlocked, though the card in the graveyard is
# the very one that would have had Annex's door had it been cast. Mox Ruby pays for the Looting; Black Lotus and Mox Emerald for the
# Woodland's {2}{G}{G}.

[Bot1 Deck]
Shifting Woodland
Mox Ruby
Faithless Looting
Unholy Annex // Ritual Chamber
Black Lotus
Mox Emerald
Swamp
Swamp x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Shifting Woodland.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Faithless Looting.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Choose(Unholy Annex // Ritual Chamber; Swamp)
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Green)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Shifting Woodland.Activate(Bot1.Graveyard.Unholy Annex // Ritual Chamber; Ability: Delirium)
[T1 Bot1.Main2]
? Bot1.Battlefield..Doors.Count = 0
